Court Dimensions, Specifications & Surface Facts

## Court Dimensions (Length × Width)

**Maximum / official size (established 1918, unchanged since):**
- 94 ft × 50 ft (≈ 28.65 m × 15.24 m) [S1]
- Confirmed as the "official court width" of 15 m in a 2018 study [S4]
- Used by college teams in Indiana and the Big Ten Intercollegiate Conference [S8]

**Minimum size court:**
- 60 ft × 35 ft [S1]

**Other sizes in use (1944):**
- 74 ft × 50 ft – regulation size for secondary schools in Indiana [S8]
- 70 ft × 40 ft – comparable to smaller secondary schools without modern gymnasiums [S8]

**Small-sided / modified courts (research contexts):**
- 15 × 6 m, 22 × 8 m, 24 × 11 m, 26.13 m, 28.15 m [S2]
- 14 m width (SSG) vs. 15 m official width – only a 1 m difference [S4]

## Key Floor Markings & Their History

| Year | Marking | Detail |
|------|---------|--------|
| ~1894 | Free-throw line | Placed 20 ft from the goal [S1] |
| 1895 | Free-throw line moved | Shifted to 15 ft from the goal; unchanged to the present [S1] |
| 1922 | Goal zone line | Extension of the free-throw line to the side lines; two-free-throw penalty for defensive fouls in that area [S1] |
| 1923 | Goal zone line discarded | Stipulation removed from the rules [S1] |
| 1932 | Center line | Divided court into front and back court; established to enforce the "ten-second" rule [S1] |

After 1932, "there has been little change in basketball courts" [S1].

## Court Surface / Flooring Specifications (FIBA 2022, Level 2)

The FIBA Official Basketball Rules 2022 set the following performance properties for permanent and mobile flooring [S10]:

| Property | Standard | Requirement |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| Force reduction | EN 14808 | Point Elastic 25–75 %; Mixed Elastic 45–75 %; Area Elastic 40–75 %; Combined Elastic 45–75 % |
| Vertical deformation | EN 14809 | Point/Mixed Elastic < 3.5 mm; Area/Combined Elastic 1.5–5.0 mm |
| Ball rebound | EN 12235 | ≥ 90 % |
| Slip resistance | EN 13036 | < 110 < 1,000 mg; Average ≥ 80 |
| Resistance to wear | EN 5470 | < 1,000 mg |
| Rolling load | EN 1569 | Permanent indentation < 0.5 mm |
| Specular gloss | – | N/A (not specified) |

Additional notes from the same source:
- High-gloss alternatives are permitted **only** when lighting is positioned to avoid unwanted court glare [S10].
- Annex 1 provides a grid-point layout for calculations and typical camera positions; Annex 2 gives recommendations for lighting positions [S10].

